# Session R (2026-06-02): de-misdirect the web_answer tool description so it stops
# steering list/research queries toward web_search.
#
# File: plugins/web-answer/tools.py  (WEB_ANSWER_SCHEMA["description"])
#
# The original description told the model to use web_answer for a "direct answer
# rather than a list of links (use web_search for links)" — which actively routed
# list-type and research queries to web_search (the wrong tool). The parenthetical
# is removed and replaced with wording that makes web_answer the choice for lists/
# breakdowns/research, reserving web_search for raw links the user wants to click.
#
# NOTE: the PRIMARY fix is the directive system_prompt (Session S). This description
# tweak is a secondary reinforcement. web_search cannot be cleanly disabled (see
# README) — the lever is wording, not tool removal.

--- a/plugins/web-answer/tools.py
+++ b/plugins/web-answer/tools.py
@@ WEB_ANSWER_SCHEMA["description"] @@
         "needs current real-world facts (product specs, prices, recent events, "
         "\"what is X\", \"how does Y compare to Z\") and wants a direct answer rather "
-        "than a list of links (use web_search for links) or the contents of one "
+        "than only a list of links — web_answer also handles lists, breakdowns, "
+        "comparisons, and research that need real data, not just headlines "
+        "(reserve web_search for when the user wants raw links to click). For the "
+        "contents of one "
         "specific URL (use web_extract). Returns a written answer followed by the "
         "sources it cites. Synthesis can take 20-40 seconds."
